        "path": "_m/g/c/s/u/laxey-wheel-wp/hero.jpg",
        "filename": "\"Elaborate technical wheel\" is of course the Laxey Wheel, Isle of Man (28289508994).jpg",
        "caption": "We continue today on the magical, mystery tour of the Mason catalogue.  An \"Elaborate technical wheel, possibly hydro electric generator, figures ascending\" a spiral staircase no less - shouldn't be too hard to identify...?\n....And indeed many immediately recognised this as the Laxey Wheel on the Isle of Man. Built in the 1850s, it was designed to pump water from the Laxey mine - and is now something of a symbol of the island.\nPhotographer:  Thomas H. Mason\nCollection:  Mason Photographic Collection\nDate: Circa 1890 - 1910\nNLI Ref:  M50/18\n\nYou can also view this image, and many thousands of others, on the NLI’s catalogue at catalogue.nli.ie",
        "alt": "We continue today on the magical, mystery tour of the Mason catalogue.  An \"Elaborate technical wheel, possibly hydro electric generator, figures ascending\" a spiral staircase no less - shouldn't be too hard to identify...?\n....And indeed many immediately recognised this as the Laxey Wheel on the Isle of Man. Built in the 1850s, it was designed to pump water from the Laxey mine - and is now something of a symbol of the island.\nPhotographer:  Thomas H. Mason\nCollection:  Mason Photographic Collection\nDate: Circa 1890 - 1910\nNLI Ref:  M50/18\n\nYou can also view this image, and many thousands of others, on the NLI’s catalogue at catalogue.nli.ie",
        "width": 2000,
        "height": 2000,
        "mimeType": "image/jpeg",
        "license": "Public domain",
        "artist": "National Library of Ireland on The Commons",
