          "path": "_m/g/c/s/u/laxey-wheel-wp/lady-isabella-geograph-org-uk--1.jpg",
          "filename": "Lady Isabella - geograph.org.uk - 1117924.jpg",
          "caption": "Lady Isabella Looking south-east down the Laxey Glen. The spiral staircase takes visitors to the top of the wheel. An enclosed pipe within the tower takes the water supply to the top. The waterwheel crank is connected to the pumping rod, which is supported on rollers along the small viaduct off to the left. The crank is also connected to the counter weight, which hangs off the front of the wheel housing on the right.",
